# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Host Type"
msgstr "Hosttype"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Orca Slicer can upload G-code files to a printer host. This field must "
"contain the kind of the host."
msgstr ""
"Orca Slicer kan G-codebestanden uploaden naar een printerhost. Dit veld moet "
"het type host bevatten."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Nozzle volume"
msgstr "Mondstuk volume"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Volume of nozzle between the filament cutter and the end of the nozzle"
msgstr ""
"Volume van het mondstuk tussen de filamentsnijder en het uiteinde van het "
"mondstuk"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Cooling tube position"
msgstr "Koelbuispositie"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Distance of the center-point of the cooling tube from the extruder tip."
msgstr "Afstand vanaf het mondstuk tot het middelpunt van de koelbuis."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Cooling tube length"
msgstr "Koelbuislengte"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Length of the cooling tube to limit space for cooling moves inside it."
msgstr ""
"Lengte van de koelbuis om de ruimte voor koelbewegingen daarin te beperken."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "High extruder current on filament swap"
msgstr "Hoge stroomsterkte bij extruder voor filamentwissel"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"It may be beneficial to increase the extruder motor current during the "
"filament exchange sequence to allow for rapid ramming feed rates and to "
"overcome resistance when loading a filament with an ugly shaped tip."
msgstr ""
"Het kan nuttig zijn om de stroomsterkte van de extrudermotor te verhogen "
"tijdens het uitvoeren van de filamentwisseling om snelle ramming mogelijk te "
"maken en om weerstand te overwinnen tijdens het laden van filament met een "
"misvormde kop."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Filament parking position"
msgstr "Filament parkeerpositie"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Distance of the extruder tip from the position where the filament is parked "
"when unloaded. This should match the value in printer firmware."
msgstr ""
"Afstand van de punt van het mondstuk tot de positie waar het filament wordt "
"geparkeerd wanneer dat niet geladen is. Deze moet overeenkomen met de waarde "
"in de firmware."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Extra loading distance"
msgstr "Extra laadafstand"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"When set to zero, the distance the filament is moved from parking position "
"during load is exactly the same as it was moved back during unload. When "
"positive, it is loaded further, if negative, the loading move is shorter "
"than unloading."
msgstr ""
"Als dit ingesteld is op 0, zal de afstand die het filament tijdens het laden "
"uit de parkeerpositie even groot zijn als wanneer het filament "
"teruggetrokken wordt. Als de waarde positief is, zal het verder geladen "
"worden. Als het negatief is, is de laadafstand dus korter."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Start end points"
msgstr "Start- en eindpunten"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"The start and end points which are from the cutter area to the excess chute."
msgstr ""
"Het begin- en eindpunt dat zich van het snijoppervlak naar de afvoer chute "
"bevindt."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Reduce infill retraction"
msgstr "Reduceer terugtrekken (retraction) bij vulling (infill)"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Don't retract when the travel is entirely within an infill area. That means "
"the oozing can't been seen. This can reduce times of retraction for complex "
"model and save printing time, but make slicing and G-code generating "
"slower.\n"
"\n"
"Note that Z-hop is also not performed in areas where retraction is skipped."
msgstr ""
"Trek niet terug als de beweging zich volledig in een opvulgebied bevindt. "
"Dat betekent dat het sijpelen niet zichtbaar is. Dit kan de retraction times "
"voor complexe modellen verkorten en printtijd besparen, maar het segmenteren "
"en het genereren van G-codes langzamer maken.\n"
"\n"
"Let op: Z-hop wordt ook niet uitgevoerd in gebieden waar het terugtrekken "
"wordt overgeslagen."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"This option will drop the temperature of the inactive extruders to prevent "
"oozing."
msgstr ""
"Deze optie verlaagt de temperatuur van de inactieve extruders om druipen te "
"voorkomen."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Filename format"
msgstr "Bestandsnaam formaat"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Users can decide project file names when exporting."
msgstr ""
"Gebruikers kunnen zelf de project bestandsnaam kiezen tijdens het exporteren"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Make overhangs printable"
msgstr "Overhangen printbaar maken"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Modify the geometry to print overhangs without support material."
msgstr ""
"Wijzig de geometrie om overhangen zonder ondersteuningsmateriaal te printen."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Make overhangs printable - Maximum angle"
msgstr "Overhangen printbaar maken - Maximale hoek"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Maximum angle of overhangs to allow after making more steep overhangs "
"printable.90° will not change the model at all and allow any overhang, while "
"0 will replace all overhangs with conical material."
msgstr ""
"Maximale hoek van overhangen die is toegestaan nadat steilere overhangen "
"printbaar zijn gemaakt. 90° verandert het model helemaal niet en staat elke "
"overhang toe, terwijl 0 alle overhangen vervangt door kegelvormig materiaal."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Make overhangs printable - Hole area"
msgstr "Overhangen printbaar maken - Gatoppervlak"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Maximum area of a hole in the base of the model before it's filled by "
"conical material. A value of 0 will fill all the holes in the model base."
msgstr ""
"Maximaal oppervlak van een gat in de basis van het model voordat het met "
"kegelvormig materiaal wordt gevuld. Bij een waarde van 0 worden alle gaten "
"in de basis van het model gevuld."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Detect overhang walls"
msgstr "Overhange wand detecteren"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
#, no-c-format, no-boost-format
msgid ""
"This detects the overhang percentage relative to line width and uses a "
"different speed to print. For 100% overhang, bridging speed is used."
msgstr ""
"Dit maakt het mogelijk om het overhangpercentage ten opzichte van de "
"lijnbreedte te detecteren en gebruikt verschillende snelheden om af te "
"drukken. Voor 100% overhang wordt de brugsnelheid gebruikt."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Print unsupported walls last"
msgstr "Niet-ondersteunde wanden als laatste printen"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Wall loops that lie entirely in mid air are printed once something can hold "
"them:\n"
"they are extruded after the other walls of their island, innermost first, "
"whatever the wall order is.\n"
"A loop that only the bridges of this layer can anchor waits until those "
"bridges are printed, while a loop running alongside a supported wall keeps "
"its place before the infill, which needs it as an anchor."
msgstr ""
"Wandlussen die volledig in de lucht liggen, worden pas geprint zodra iets ze "
"kan dragen:\n"
"ze worden geëxtrudeerd na de andere wanden van hun eiland, de binnenste "
"eerst, ongeacht de wandvolgorde.\n"
"Een lus die alleen de bruggen van deze laag kunnen verankeren, wacht tot die "
"bruggen geprint zijn, terwijl een lus die langs een ondersteunde wand loopt "
"zijn plek vóór de vulling behoudt, die hem als verankering nodig heeft."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Outer walls"
msgstr "Buitenste wanden"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Filament to print outer walls.\n"
"\"Default\" uses the active object/part filament."
msgstr ""
"Filament om de buitenste wanden te printen.\n"
"\"Standaard\" gebruikt het filament van het actieve object/onderdeel."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Inner walls"
msgstr "Binnenste wanden"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Filament to print inner walls.\n"
"\"Default\" uses the active object/part filament."
msgstr ""
"Filament om de binnenste wanden te printen.\n"
"\"Standaard\" gebruikt het filament van het actieve object/onderdeel."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Line width of inner wall. If expressed as a %, it will be computed over the "
"nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""
"Lijnbreedte van de binnenste wand. Als dit als % wordt uitgedrukt, wordt het "
"berekend over de mondstukdiameter."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "This is the speed for inner walls."
msgstr "Dit is de snelheid voor de binnenste wanden"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "This is the number of walls per layer."
msgstr "Dit is het aantal wanden per laag."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Alternate extra wall"
msgstr "Afwisselende extra wand"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"This setting adds an extra wall to every other layer. This way the infill "
"gets wedged vertically between the walls, resulting in stronger prints.\n"
"\n"
"When this option is enabled, the ensure vertical shell thickness option "
"needs to be disabled.\n"
"\n"
"Using lightning infill together with this option is not recommended as there "
"is limited infill to anchor the extra perimeters to."
msgstr ""
"Deze instelling voegt om de andere laag een extra wand toe. Zo wordt de "
"vulling verticaal tussen de wanden geklemd, wat sterkere prints oplevert.\n"
"\n"
"Wanneer deze optie is ingeschakeld, moet de optie voor het waarborgen van de "
"verticale wanddikte worden uitgeschakeld.\n"
"\n"
"Het gebruik van Lightning-vulling in combinatie met deze optie wordt "
"afgeraden, omdat er weinig vulling is om de extra perimeters aan te "
"verankeren."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"If you want to process the output G-code through custom scripts, just list "
"their absolute paths here. Separate multiple scripts with a semicolon. "
"Scripts will be passed the absolute path to the G-code file as the first "
"argument, and they can access the Orca Slicer config settings by reading "
"environment variables."
msgstr ""
"Als u de uitvoer-G-code door aangepaste scripts wilt laten verwerken, geef "
"hier dan hun absolute paden op. Scheid meerdere scripts met een puntkomma. "
"De scripts krijgen het absolute pad naar het G-code-bestand als eerste "
"argument en kunnen de configuratie-instellingen van Orca Slicer benaderen "
"door omgevingsvariabelen te lezen."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Change extrusion role G-code (process)"
msgstr "G-code bij wijzigen van extrusietype (proces)"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"This G-code is inserted when the extrusion role is changed. It runs after "
"the machine and filament extrusion role G-code."
msgstr ""
"Deze G-code wordt ingevoegd wanneer het extrusietype wijzigt. Hij wordt "
"uitgevoerd na de G-code voor het extrusietype van de machine en het filament."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Plugins Used"
msgstr "Gebruikte plug-ins"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Plugin capabilities referenced by this preset, stored as "
"name;uuid;capability."
msgstr ""
"Plug-inmogelijkheden waarnaar deze voorinstelling verwijst, opgeslagen als "
"name;uuid;capability."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Python plugins invoked at each slicing pipeline step to read and modify "
"intermediate slicing data, including a final G-code post-processing step. "
"Research/experimental."
msgstr ""
"Python-plug-ins die bij elke stap van de slicepijplijn worden aangeroepen om "
"tussentijdse slicegegevens te lezen en te wijzigen, inclusief een "
"afsluitende nabewerkingsstap voor de G-code. Onderzoek/experimenteel."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Printer type"
msgstr "Printertype"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Type of the printer."
msgstr "Type van de printer."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Printer notes"
msgstr "Printernotities"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "You can put your notes regarding the printer here."
msgstr "Hier kunt u uw notities over de printer plaatsen."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Printer variant"
msgstr "Printervariant"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Raft contact Z distance"
msgstr "Vlot (raft) contact Z afstand:"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Z gap between raft and object. If Support Top Z Distance is 0, this value is "
"ignored and the object is printed in direct contact with the raft (no gap)."
msgstr ""
"Z-gap tussen het vlot en het object. Als de bovenste Z-afstand van de "
"ondersteuning 0 is, wordt deze waarde genegeerd en wordt het object direct "
"in contact met het vlot geprint (geen gap)."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Raft expansion"
msgstr "Vlot (raft) expansie"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "This expands all raft layers in XY plane."
msgstr "Dit vergroot alle raft lagen in het XY vlak."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "First layer density"
msgstr "Dichtheid van de eerste laag"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "This is the density of the first raft or support layer."
msgstr "Dit is de dichtheid van de eerste raft- of support laag."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "First layer expansion"
msgstr "Vergroten van de eerste laag"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "This expands the first raft or support layer to improve bed adhesion."
msgstr ""
"Dit zet de eerste raft- of steun (support) laag uit om de hechting van het "
"bed te verbeteren."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Raft layers"
msgstr "Vlot (raft) lagen"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Object will be raised by this number of support layers. Use this function to "
"avoid warping when printing ABS."
msgstr ""
"Het object wordt verhoogd met dit aantal support lagen. Gebruik deze functie "
"om kromtrekken te voorkomen bij het afdrukken met ABS."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"The G-code path is generated after simplifying the contour of models to "
"avoid too many points and G-code lines. Smaller values mean higher "
"resolution and more time required to slice."
msgstr ""
"Het G-codepad wordt gegenereerd na het vereenvoudigen van de contouren van "
"modellen om teveel punten en G-codelijnen te vermijden. Kleinere waarden "
"betekenen een hogere resolutie en meer tijd die nodig is om het ontwerpen te "
"slicen."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Travel distance threshold"
msgstr "Drempel voor verplaatsingsafstand"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Only trigger retraction when the travel distance is longer than this "
"threshold."
msgstr ""
"Activeer het terugtrekken (retraction) alleen als de verplaatsingsafstand "
"groter is dan deze drempel."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Retract amount before wipe"
msgstr "Terugtrek (retract) hoeveelheid voor schoonvegen"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"This is the length of fast retraction before a wipe, relative to retraction "
"length."
msgstr ""
"Dit is de lengte van snel intrekken (retraction) vóór een wipe, in "
"verhouding tot de retraction lengte."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Retract amount after wipe"
msgstr "Terugtrekhoeveelheid na vegen"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
#, no-c-format, no-boost-format
msgid ""
"This is the length of fast retraction after wipe, relative to retraction "
"length.\n"
"The value will be clamped by 100% minus the retract amount before the wipe "
"value."
msgstr ""
"De lengte van de snelle terugtrekking na het vegen, relatief ten opzichte "
"van de terugtreklengte.\n"
"De waarde wordt begrensd op 100% min de waarde van de terugtrekhoeveelheid "
"vóór het vegen."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Retract on layer change"
msgstr "Terugtrekken (retract) bij wisselen van laag"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "This forces a retraction on layer changes."
msgstr ""
"Dit forceert retraction (terugtrekken van filament) als er gewisseld wordt "
"van laag"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Retraction Length"
msgstr "Terugtrek (retraction) lengte"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Some amount of material in extruder is pulled back to avoid ooze during long "
"travel. Set zero to disable retraction."
msgstr ""
"Er wordt een hoeveelheid materiaal in de extruder teruggetrokken om druipen "
"tijdens lange verplaatsingen te voorkomen. Zet op nul om terugtrekken "
"(retraction) uit te schakelen."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Long retraction when cut (beta)"
msgstr "Lange terugtrekking bij afsnijden (bèta)"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Experimental feature: Retracting and cutting off the filament at a longer "
"distance during changes to minimize purge. While this reduces flush "
"significantly, it may also raise the risk of nozzle clogs or other printing "
"problems."
msgstr ""
"Experimentele functie: Het filament wordt tijdens het wisselen over een "
"grotere afstand teruggetrokken en afgesneden om de spoeling tot een minimum "
"te beperken. Dit vermindert de spoeling aanzienlijk, maar vergroot mogelijk "
"ook het risico op verstoppingen in het mondstuk of andere printproblemen."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Retraction distance when cut"
msgstr "Terugtrekafstand bij afsnijden"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Experimental feature: Retraction length before cutting off during filament "
"change."
msgstr ""
"Experimentele functie: terugtreklengte voordat er tijdens een filamentwissel "
"wordt afgesneden."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Long retraction when extruder change"
msgstr "Lange terugtrekking bij extruderwissel"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Retraction distance when extruder change"
msgstr "Terugtrekafstand bij extruderwissel"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Retraction Length (Toolchange)"
msgstr "Terugtreklengte (Gereedschapswissel)"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"When retraction is triggered before changing tool, filament is pulled back "
"by the specified amount (the length is measured on raw filament, before it "
"enters the extruder)."
msgstr ""
"Wanneer het terugtrekken vóór een gereedschapswissel wordt geactiveerd, "
"wordt het filament met de opgegeven hoeveelheid teruggetrokken (de lengte "
"wordt gemeten op het onbewerkte filament, voordat het de extruder ingaat)."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Z-hop height"
msgstr "Z-hop-hoogte"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Whenever there is a retraction, the nozzle is lifted a little to create "
"clearance between the nozzle and the print. This prevents the nozzle from "
"hitting the print when traveling more. Using spiral lines to lift Z can "
"prevent stringing."
msgstr ""
"Wanneer er een terugtrekking (retraction) is, wordt het mondstuk een beetje "
"opgetild om ruimte te creëren tussen het mondstuk en de print. Dit voorkomt "
"dat het mondstuk de print raakt bij verplaatsen. Het gebruik van "
"spiraallijnen om Z op te tillen kan stringing voorkomen."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Z-hop lower boundary"
msgstr "Z-hop ondergrens"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Z-hop will only come into effect when Z is above this value and is below the "
"parameter: \"Z-hop upper boundary\"."
msgstr ""
"Z-hop treedt alleen in werking wanneer Z boven deze waarde ligt en onder de "
"parameter: \"Z-hop bovengrens\"."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Z-hop upper boundary"
msgstr "Z-hop bovengrens"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"If this value is positive, Z-hop will only come into effect when Z is above "
"the parameter: \"Z-hop lower boundary\" and is below this value."
msgstr ""
"Als deze waarde positief is, treedt Z-hop alleen in werking als Z boven de "
"parameter ligt: \"Z-hop ondergrens\" en onder deze waarde ligt"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Z-hop type"
msgstr "Z-hop-type"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Type of Z-hop."
msgstr "Type Z-hop."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Normal"
msgstr "Normaal"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Slope"
msgstr "Helling"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Spiral"
msgstr "Spiraal"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Traveling angle"
msgstr "Verplaatsingshoek"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"Traveling angle for Slope and Spiral Z-hop type. Setting it to 90° results "
"in Normal Lift."
msgstr ""
"Verplaatsingshoek voor de Z-hop-types Helling en Spiraal. Bij 90° ontstaat "
"een normale lift."

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid "Only lift Z above"
msgstr "Beweeg Z alleen omhoog boven"

# Needs human review: copied from the nl catalogue, check it reads right for nl_BE
msgid ""
"If you set this to a positive value, Z lift will only take place above the "
"specified absolute Z."
msgstr ""
